wip/paraview: update to 6.2.0; enable Qt6, Python, MPI and OSPRay

Build the Qt6 GUI, Python (pvpython/pvbatch with NumPy), MPI (via
mk/mpi.buildlink3.mk), OSPRay ray tracing (wip/ospray), Viskores with
the TBB backend (TBB is also the VTK SMP backend), FFmpeg (ffmpeg7)
movie writing, XDMF2/3, CGNS and the VisIt readers.  Take expat,
freetype, jpeg, libxml2, lz4, xz, png, tiff, zlib and eigen from
pkgsrc; HDF5, NetCDF, CGNS, Exodus and IOSS stay bundled.

On Darwin the GUI is installed as ${PREFIX}/Applications/paraview.app
with a launcher in bin, rendering through Cocoa/OpenGL (Apple's
OpenGL 4.1 on Metal); X11 libraries are only used elsewhere.

New patches:
- give plugin libraries an absolute install name instead of
  @loader_path, which pkg_add cannot resolve in REQUIRES;
- disable OSPRay 3.2 MIP-map generation, which made scalar colouring
  (VTK's 258x2 colour-map texture) banded and washed out.
The ioss statvfs patch is now NetBSD-only (it broke Darwin).

Catalyst (catalyst library not packaged), the web/wslink support and
the WebGPU backend (VTK needs Dawn, not wgpu-native) stay off.
